      "fieldData": {
       "alpb---prompt": "<p>Build a vocabulary quiz that collects every answer in a database I own.</p><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbPrompt = {\"default\": \"Build a vocabulary quiz that collects every answer in a database I own.\", \"chips\": [{\"label\": \"Weekly Word List\", \"add\": \"Add a weekly word list quiz that shows which words each class missed.\"}, {\"label\": \"Spanish Words\", \"add\": \"Add a quiz on Spanish words that matches each one to its English meaning.\"}, {\"label\": \"SAT Word Practice\", \"add\": \"Add SAT word practice with 15 words a week and a score history per student.\"}, {\"label\": \"Adult Learners\", \"add\": \"Add a version for adult learners that shows one question per screen on a phone.\"}]}; </script></div></div><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script id='awb-quiz-data'> window.awbQuiz = {\"version\":1,\"type\":\"knowledge\",\"title\":\"Vocabulary Quiz: 8 Words, How Many Do You Know?\",\"intro\":\"Eight questions on everyday words that show up in books, news, and class. Pick one answer per question; your score and the meanings show at the end.\",\"questions\":[{\"text\":\"A flower that blooms for a single morning could be called ephemeral. What does ephemeral mean?\",\"options\":[{\"text\":\"Fleeting or short-lived\",\"correct\":true},{\"text\":\"Brightly colored\"},{\"text\":\"Grown from a seed\"},{\"text\":\"Sweet smelling\"}],\"explanation\":\"Ephemeral describes anything that does not last: a pop-up shop, a snowman, a trend that fades in a week.\",\"source\":{\"url\":\"https://www.vocabulary.com/dictionary/ephemeral\",\"quote\":\"Something that is fleeting or short-lived is ephemeral\"}},{\"text\":\"A friend gives you a candid opinion of your essay. What kind of opinion is it?\",\"options\":[{\"text\":\"Polite and vague\"},{\"text\":\"Straightforward and truthful\",\"correct\":true},{\"text\":\"Short and rushed\"},{\"text\":\"Written in secret\"}],\"explanation\":\"A candid answer says what the speaker really thinks, even when the listener would rather hear praise.\",\"source\":{\"url\":\"https://www.vocabulary.com/dictionary/candid\",\"quote\":\"Straightforward and truthful talk might be described with the adjective candid\"}},{\"text\":\"Which phrase describes a frugal person?\",\"options\":[{\"text\":\"Lives simply and economically\",\"correct\":true},{\"text\":\"Gives generous gifts\"},{\"text\":\"Travels on short notice\"},{\"text\":\"Keeps a strict schedule\"}],\"explanation\":\"Frugal is about careful spending, such as buying clothes secondhand. It is a kinder word than cheap.\",\"source\":{\"url\":\"https://www.vocabulary.com/dictionary/frugal\",\"quote\":\"A person who lives simply and economically can be called frugal\"}},{\"text\":\"What does tenacious mean in the sentence \\\"She kept a tenacious grip on the rope\\\"?\",\"options\":[{\"text\":\"Loose and careless\"},{\"text\":\"Not easily letting go or giving up\",\"correct\":true},{\"text\":\"Shaking with fear\"},{\"text\":\"Quick to react\"}],\"explanation\":\"Tenacious comes up for grips and for people. A tenacious student keeps working on a problem until it gives way.\",\"source\":{\"url\":\"https://www.vocabulary.com/dictionary/tenacious\",\"quote\":\"not easily letting go or giving up\"}},{\"text\":\"A headline can be read two different ways. Which word describes it?\",\"options\":[{\"text\":\"Concise\"},{\"text\":\"Ambiguous\",\"correct\":true},{\"text\":\"Sarcastic\"},{\"text\":\"Outdated\"}],\"explanation\":\"Something ambiguous is open to more than one interpretation, so the reader has to guess which meaning was intended.\",\"source\":{\"url\":\"https://www.vocabulary.com/dictionary/ambiguous\",\"quote\":\"Look to the adjective ambiguous when you need to describe something that's open to more than one interpretation\"}},{\"text\":\"A neighbor shovels snow for the whole street. Which phrase explains why that is benevolent?\",\"options\":[{\"text\":\"Does good deeds or shows goodwill\",\"correct\":true},{\"text\":\"Follows every rule exactly\"},{\"text\":\"Works hard in bad weather\"},{\"text\":\"Wants to be noticed\"}],\"explanation\":\"Benevolent fits kindness offered freely, like clearing a path nobody asked for.\",\"source\":{\"url\":\"https://www.vocabulary.com/dictionary/benevolent\",\"quote\":\"for someone who does good deeds or shows goodwill\"}},{\"text\":\"Phones seem to be in every pocket and on every table. Which word fits that idea?\",\"options\":[{\"text\":\"Ubiquitous\",\"correct\":true},{\"text\":\"Obsolete\"},{\"text\":\"Fragile\"},{\"text\":\"Expensive\"}],\"explanation\":\"Ubiquitous means present in all places at the same time, or close enough that it feels that way.\",\"source\":{\"url\":\"https://www.vocabulary.com/dictionary/ubiquitous\",\"quote\":\"present in all places at the same time, reach for the adjective ubiquitous\"}},{\"text\":\"A teacher calls a book report verbose. What is the report doing?\",\"options\":[{\"text\":\"Leaves out the ending\"},{\"text\":\"Goes on and on\",\"correct\":true},{\"text\":\"Copies the back cover\"},{\"text\":\"Uses too few examples\"}],\"explanation\":\"A verbose report uses far more words than it needs. Cutting it in half makes the point easier to find.\",\"source\":{\"url\":\"https://www.vocabulary.com/dictionary/verbose\",\"quote\":\"A verbose book report goes on and on\"}}],\"results\":[{\"key\":\"keep-building\",\"title\":\"Keep Building Your Word Bank\",\"min\":0,\"max\":3,\"description\":\"A few of these words were new to you, and that is the point of a quiz. Open the answers below, read each example sentence, and try the quiz again tomorrow to see which words stuck.\"},{\"key\":\"growing-range\",\"title\":\"Your Range Is Growing\",\"min\":4,\"max\":6,\"description\":\"You knew most of the everyday words. Check the answers below for the ones that slipped, then use each of them in a sentence of your own this week.\"},{\"key\":\"word-ready\",\"title\":\"Ready for Harder Words\",\"min\":7,\"max\":8,\"description\":\"You matched almost every word to its meaning. Try a harder list next, with words like laconic, obstinate, and gregarious.\"}]}; </script></div></div>",
